                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6337fa05-8316-3933-ac5d-50b1571d7ffe",
                        "entry_id": "7cabee63-e9a7-3dbf-8cc5-bcb6edfbc197",
                        "glosses": [
                            "de of een universiteit betreffende"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fe77c96e-8856-4abc-8782-3cfa5ea5bafa",
                                "sense_id": "6337fa05-8316-3933-ac5d-50b1571d7ffe",
                                "text": "Hij kreeg hierdoor te maken met onder meer doodsbedreigingen en bommeldingen op de faculteit. In 2009 blikte de criminoloog in gesprek met het Leids Universitair Weekblad Mare terug op die periode. \"Ik schermde zo goed mogelijk mijn gezin af, maar dat lukte natuurlijk slecht.\" Zo kreeg hij ook telefonisch bedreigingen en werd er poep door de brievenbus gegooid."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b826a14b-9a6c-4c08-a5fb-4990d57dc8f2",
                                "sense_id": "6337fa05-8316-3933-ac5d-50b1571d7ffe",
                                "text": "Maar waarom zijn juist kinderen zo interessant voor sociale media? Dat heeft alles te maken met adverteerders. Die zijn op zoek naar een jonge doelgroep en die vinden ze op sociale media, legt universitair hoofddocent communicatiewetenschap aan de Universiteit van Amsterdam Eva van Reijmersdal uit."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c5883b65-610e-47a1-af34-3a6fed697d45",
                        "source_entry_id": "7cabee63-e9a7-3dbf-8cc5-bcb6edfbc197",
                        "source_sense_id": "6337fa05-8316-3933-ac5d-50b1571d7ffe",
                        "target_lang_word": "academic",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "academic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "16c15c25-4466-3097-bf8b-5081b25cb4e9",
                                        "entry_id": "dc0444f9-bcbd-3b2d-8eb8-2f81ed0b4a4c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Belonging to the school or philosophy of Plato."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d36e88ff-c026-489c-a2b7-73e63d208d60",
                                                "sense_id": "16c15c25-4466-3097-bf8b-5081b25cb4e9",
                                                "text": "the academic sect or philosophy"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "75c3e834-3395-3273-abcc-789fa27eede6",
                                        "entry_id": "dc0444f9-bcbd-3b2d-8eb8-2f81ed0b4a4c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Belonging to an academy or other higher institution of learning, or a scholarly society or organization."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74ace173-0cea-4ef6-988b-d31d1a8cb657",
                                                "sense_id": "75c3e834-3395-3273-abcc-789fa27eede6",
                                                "text": "But unhappily, by too short a view of things, you have been apt to mistake the completion of your academic courses for the completion of your theologic studies: and then, by a false modesty, have despaired of knowing more than you would suffer those august places of your education to teach you."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5124e2f9-c015-4254-a304-e1ab1b9c2846",
                                                "sense_id": "75c3e834-3395-3273-abcc-789fa27eede6",
                                                "text": "It was left to the motor industry, half a century later, to destroy Oxford's academic calm."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d4ffbeea-b9b4-3a7f-8820-af068b8fa4fc",
                                        "entry_id": "dc0444f9-bcbd-3b2d-8eb8-2f81ed0b4a4c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In particular: relating to literary, classical, or artistic studies like the humanities, rather than to technical or vocational studies like engineering or welding."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "86381aaf-209d-4794-ba0c-638faeb50612",
                                                "sense_id": "d4ffbeea-b9b4-3a7f-8820-af068b8fa4fc",
                                                "text": "Programs of work should provide students the opportunities to demonstrate both academic and vocational competence attainment."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "03f0bc1c-b5be-4bcf-ba10-a37b89b71e1a",
                                                "sense_id": "d4ffbeea-b9b4-3a7f-8820-af068b8fa4fc",
                                                "text": "Evidence for cannibalism abounds - even if circumstantial - both from the modern world and throughout history, but academic anthropology has found itself in a funk of denial."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1e9ccb46-31cc-3a04-91ee-34bb64656f99",
                                        "entry_id": "dc0444f9-bcbd-3b2d-8eb8-2f81ed0b4a4c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having little practical use or value, as by being overly detailed and unengaging, or by being theoretical and speculative with no practical importance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f8ae297f-7eae-4e49-8f88-f9a81bcc82e5",
                                                "sense_id": "1e9ccb46-31cc-3a04-91ee-34bb64656f99",
                                                "text": "an academic question"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6a7a8d7a-f178-477a-a11b-8490367f5c5d",
                                                "sense_id": "1e9ccb46-31cc-3a04-91ee-34bb64656f99",
                                                "text": "I have always had an academic interest in hacking."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e23cb92e-505d-4245-b52d-2a1fd7d2aee9",
                                                "sense_id": "1e9ccb46-31cc-3a04-91ee-34bb64656f99",
                                                "text": "the distinction is academic"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f4958c09-3be6-49b6-af53-2a4ec2612029",
                                                "sense_id": "1e9ccb46-31cc-3a04-91ee-34bb64656f99",
                                                "text": "The character of the process by which the views of the intellectuals influence the politics of tomorrow is therefore of much more than academic interest."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d503df11-a69d-4d1c-b9f2-0f5f3d5613e0",
                                                "sense_id": "1e9ccb46-31cc-3a04-91ee-34bb64656f99",
                                                "text": "The exact sequence and timing of the subsequent explosions and inflight fires are not known and are, in fact, somewhat academic with respect to the probable cause of the accident."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a48b4748-d848-49f6-8323-873f446a2386",
                                                "sense_id": "1e9ccb46-31cc-3a04-91ee-34bb64656f99",
                                                "text": "But almost always such words are irreversibly established before the objectors learn of their existence, and the objections are hardly more than academic exercises."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7ea55b16-4b49-4068-80d0-5d70c93cd5a1",
                                                "sense_id": "1e9ccb46-31cc-3a04-91ee-34bb64656f99",
                                                "text": "In theory, a fully intact reverse osmosis membrane should be capable of removing lipopolysaccharide pyrogens […] In practice, this distinction is academic, because pyrogens do not replicate, and as long as the product water is […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8913030e-dd2e-4944-84d6-3889dada6ae0",
                                                "sense_id": "1e9ccb46-31cc-3a04-91ee-34bb64656f99",
                                                "text": "In practice this distinction is academic, as any small nodule on the surface of a thyroidectomy specimen should be examined histologically. If carcinoma is suspected or proven, the whole surface of the specimen may be marked[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "043757c3-0463-46e3-9ebc-c947ce48e324",
                                                "sense_id": "1e9ccb46-31cc-3a04-91ee-34bb64656f99",
                                                "text": "The question of how many weapons are required for credible deterrence against India is purely academic."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b963fcc1-1bef-4ce5-93e5-57944f6f9a05",
                                                "sense_id": "1e9ccb46-31cc-3a04-91ee-34bb64656f99",
                                                "text": "For the majority of owners, its four-wheel-drive endeavours will be of purely academic interest."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c9383de6-e8ba-4d50-a4af-90477f9d4dcb",
                                                "sense_id": "1e9ccb46-31cc-3a04-91ee-34bb64656f99",
                                                "text": "As a general matter, we will not consider a protest where the issue presented has no practical consequences with regard to an existing federal government procurement, and thus is of purely academic interest."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f1046190-ad45-4d5f-b7aa-8b1c31f274db",
                                                "sense_id": "1e9ccb46-31cc-3a04-91ee-34bb64656f99",
                                                "text": "[…]; if you do not know, or care to know, much about critical theory, the writings of Butler are academic in the unflattering sense of that term. But in their world, they are, if not royalty, lords of the realm."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "911dc339-cbca-4c07-8bd5-aa29b2e8fa7c",
                                                "sense_id": "1e9ccb46-31cc-3a04-91ee-34bb64656f99",
                                                "text": "SCP-3125 had skirmished with ω-0 before, but it had always been unclear how much information about ω-0 it retained between skirmishes. In fact it was unclear, fundamentally speaking, how SCP-3125 thought at all. Its behaviour was inconsistent, unpredictable and frightening; records of its activities were cognitohazardous, discouraging close analysis.\nIn the end, the question proved to be academic. When SCP-3125 arrived, whether it knew ω-0 was there or not, it took no special action against it, and had no need to. Most of ω-0's members' anchors were Foundationers, or Foundation-adjacent. With those people's minds blown away in the first strike, the dense web of mutual memory which had held the Task Force together since its formation tore loose. More than half of the Task Force was cast into the void and died; the final, real death they had evaded for years."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0b0818ae-6b18-36a3-996b-b0af46d859c2",
                                        "entry_id": "dc0444f9-bcbd-3b2d-8eb8-2f81ed0b4a4c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having a love of or aptitude for learning."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "68e30bf4-79ee-481a-a0f7-10b48a65d8e5",
                                                "sense_id": "0b0818ae-6b18-36a3-996b-b0af46d859c2",
                                                "text": "I’m more academic than athletic — I get lower marks in phys. ed. than in anything else."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "954828e7-d1cc-3a87-9117-c23e0ecc5d06",
                                        "entry_id": "dc0444f9-bcbd-3b2d-8eb8-2f81ed0b4a4c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Conforming to set rules and traditions; conventional; formalistic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "78e2177e-bd7e-3498-a2c0-16e55cf86715",
                                        "entry_id": "dc0444f9-bcbd-3b2d-8eb8-2f81ed0b4a4c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Conforming to set rules and traditions; conventional; formalistic.",
                                            "Subscribing to the architectural standards of Vitruvius."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "63e1defd-93b2-3fb0-bd7a-b583211ad4f2",
                                        "entry_id": "dc0444f9-bcbd-3b2d-8eb8-2f81ed0b4a4c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "So scholarly as to be unaware of the outside world; lacking in worldliness; inexperienced in practical matters."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "academic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "21d08162-73bc-31a5-bd5b-00c729a16fc3",
                                        "entry_id": "bd2a45df-b734-3a8b-876a-36be912d5832",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A follower of Plato, a Platonist."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "capitalized",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ad5836ec-7e8c-3816-bd5a-7bf0b9e0d0ab",
                                        "entry_id": "bd2a45df-b734-3a8b-876a-36be912d5832",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A senior member of an academy, college, or university; a person who attends an academy; a person engaged in scholarly pursuits; one who is academic in practice."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "06d9ebc0-bb0f-44ff-b672-9502bf13b22e",
                                                "sense_id": "ad5836ec-7e8c-3816-bd5a-7bf0b9e0d0ab",
                                                "text": "Academics[…]see integrated systems for collecting, processing and acting on data as offering a “second electrification” to the world’s metropolises."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8a91c78f-a5a5-39ac-9d59-1d09ec254ef9",
                                        "entry_id": "bd2a45df-b734-3a8b-876a-36be912d5832",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A member of the Academy; an academician."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1179a8c3-fc4a-49c9-a46c-c7e94c9b203c",
                                                "sense_id": "8a91c78f-a5a5-39ac-9d59-1d09ec254ef9",
                                                "text": "Carneades the academick, when he was to write against Zeno the stoick, purged himself with hellebor first […]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "50a6b62e-fed2-3edf-8558-09e806edd8df",
                                        "entry_id": "bd2a45df-b734-3a8b-876a-36be912d5832",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A student in a college."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2050e25c-e40a-3c9b-b73c-58e252d428be",
                                        "entry_id": "bd2a45df-b734-3a8b-876a-36be912d5832",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Academic dress; academicals."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "plural",
                                            "plural-only"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d357651d-0cb7-395f-9530-53c23e5a65cb",
                                        "entry_id": "bd2a45df-b734-3a8b-876a-36be912d5832",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Academic studies."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "plural",
                                            "plural-only"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "630b76be-4154-4e21-936c-0ae186cf7a01",
                                                "sense_id": "d357651d-0cb7-395f-9530-53c23e5a65cb",
                                                "text": "Many spoke of an intense fear of failing one’s academics at university, which can both be highly motivating to secure academic success (sometimes at the cost of socialising), but can also immobilise one’s desire to try harder as it can be rather disappointing if one does not succeed. […] Many autistic students commonly reported viewing academics to be the most important aspect of university life and had a strong sense of persistence and self-determination to succeed. […] However, while some autistic students viewed socialising to be a source of threat that could jeopardise their academic success if indulged in, others highlighted the importance of social connections at university beyond that of academics."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5cfd2886-70bb-40b1-9b86-10ced40ff10f",
                        "source_entry_id": "7cabee63-e9a7-3dbf-8cc5-bcb6edfbc197",
                        "source_sense_id": "6337fa05-8316-3933-ac5d-50b1571d7ffe",
